      "id": "medirag",
      "title": "MediRAG",
      "genre": "GenAI • RAG • Healthcare",
      "logline": "Meet Dr. Insight — a medical assistant that answers only from trusted medical documents, admits when it doesn't know, and always points you to a real doctor",
      "stack": [
        "Python",
        "Flask",
        "LangChain",
        "Mistral AI",
        "HuggingFace",
        "Pinecone"
      ],
      "build": [
        "Built a RAG-based medical QA system with LangChain retrieval chains, Mistral Large and a Pinecone serverless vector index",
        "Built the ingestion pipeline: PDF extraction with PyPDF, recursive text chunking (300 characters, 50 overlap) and HuggingFace all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings.",
        "Tuned retrieval and generation for safety: top-5 cosine similarity search, low temperature (0.2) and a system prompt that forbids fabricated facts and always recommends a doctor.",
        "Developed a Flask chat app with session-based conversation memory and a responsive chat UI with typing indicators.",
        "Short-circuited greetings with instant replies, cutting unnecessary LLM calls."
      ],
      "features": [
        "Answers grounded in medical PDFs through retrieval-augmented generation",
        "Says “I don't know” instead of guessing, and recommends a real doctor",
        "Semantic search over a Pinecone vector index (cosine, 384-dim MiniLM embeddings)",
        "Remembers the conversation, so follow-up questions just work",
        "Empathetic “Dr. Insight” persona that acknowledges feelings before facts"
